    "en": {
      "shared_perspectives": "German media across the spectrum agree that Germany’s digital infrastructure is lagging and must be accelerated, with repeated calls for massive broadband rollout, stronger cybersecurity measures and state‑backed funding for AI research and digital education. At the same time there is a broad consensus that the EU AI Act and tighter data‑protection rules are essential to curb the risks of large‑scale language models, even as outlets differ on the pace of implementation. Finally, most commentators, from left‑leaning to conservative, stress that unchecked automation will reshape the labour market and therefore requires coordinated policy responses such as upskilling programmes and safeguards for vulnerable workers.",
